# deployment.mdc — Interview Architect

```yaml
deployment:
  cloudProvider: Cloudflare Workers and Cloudflare D1

  environments:
    - name: local
      purpose: Developer workstation with local D1 migrations, Vite frontend, and Wrangler Worker API.
      runCommand: npm run dev
    - name: production
      purpose: Public portfolio deployment at interview-architect.kritikamodi.workers.dev.
      deployMechanism: Apply remote D1 migrations, then run npx wrangler deploy --config infra/wrangler.jsonc with account authorization.

  strategy:
    type: Manual Worker deployment with same-origin static assets and API.
    featureFlags: No feature-flag system is configured.

  rollback:
    code: Revert the production commit, rebuild, and redeploy the previous known-good Worker/static assets version.
    database: Use a forward corrective D1 migration; do not apply destructive rollback SQL to production without a verified recovery plan.
    config: Revert the relevant infra/wrangler.jsonc or static-header change in a dedicated commit and redeploy.

  ci:
    provider: GitHub Actions
    prChecks: content validation, typecheck, Vitest suites, production build, and Chromium Playwright E2E must pass before merge.
    watchCommand: gh pr checks {number}

  observability:
    apm: No external APM configured; use Worker health endpoint and Cloudflare dashboard/Worker logs for current operational visibility.
    logs: Sanitized application errors only; do not log session cookies, drafts, provider keys, or secrets.
```
